# Cloudflare Workers static-assets deploy uploads everything in this
# directory by default (it doesn't know which files are actually meant to
# be public web assets vs. deploy tooling) -- exclude the non-asset files
# so they aren't served at e.g. usemeritai.com/Dockerfile. Nothing in these
# was ever sensitive (all public in the repo anyway), just not meant to be
# a served URL.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluding wrangler.jsonc or .wrangler/ here -- an earlier
# version of this file did, and the very next deploy failed. Those are
# wrangler's own generated config and the no-op worker script it needs to
# actually serve static assets at all, not just extra public-facing noise
# like Dockerfile is -- excluding them broke the build, not just hid a file.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
